      "teaser": "\u003Cp\u003EThe NICE-Wide Prioritisation Board met on 16 April 2026 and concluded that an evaluation would&nbsp;\u003Cstrong\u003Enot\u003C/strong\u003E&nbsp;be appropriate&nbsp;for this product. \u003Ca href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/2024-voluntary-scheme-for-branded-medicines-pricing-access-and-growth\"\u003EThe 2024 voluntary scheme for branded medicines, pricing, access and growth\u003C/a\u003E&nbsp;states that NICE will continue to evaluate all new active substances and significant indications, except where there is a clear rationale not to do so. Decision makers concluded that the clear rationale to not evaluate&nbsp;this product is due to the proposed extension being a new dosing regimen that is not expected to impact the cost and clinical effectiveness of the published guidance within \u003Ca href=\"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ta915\"\u003ETA915\u003C/a\u003E. Please see&nbsp;\u003Ca href=\"https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg46/chapter/eligibility-criteria-for-using-the-prioritisation-framework-and-direct-routing-to-guidance\"\u003Eeligibility criteria&nbsp;\u003C/a\u003Ewithin the prioritisation manual for further information.\u003C/p\u003E",
